.TH voltkit-gpu 1  "Voltkit 0.9.2" "Manuel de Voltkit"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NOM
voltkit\-gpu \- Surveiller les cartes graphiques NVIDIA, AMD et Intel et régler leur puissance, leurs ventilateurs, leurs fréquences et leur température
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvoltkit gpu\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIcommandes\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Surveiller les cartes graphiques NVIDIA, AMD et Intel et régler leur puissance, leurs ventilateurs, leurs fréquences et leur température
.PP
Sans sous\-commande, affiche chaque carte avec ses mesures et les contrôles qu’elle prend en charge, avec la raison de ceux qu’elle ne prend pas en charge. Modifier les réglages demande les droits d’administrateur, et tout ce que vous ne confirmez pas est annulé.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Afficher l’aide (un résumé avec « \-h »)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH COMMANDES
.TP
\fBvoltkit gpu show\fR
Afficher les cartes graphiques, leurs mesures et ce que chacune permet de contrôler
.TP
\fBvoltkit gpu apply [\-\-save] [\-\-yes] [\-\-confirm]\fR
Apply GPU settings from a JSON file, undoing them unless you confirm

The file holds the settings for one card: its PCI address as "gpu", and any of "power_limit_w", "fan" ({"mode":"auto"}, {"mode":"fixed","speed_pct":50} or {"mode":"curve","points":[...]}), "temperature_target_c", "core_offset_mhz", "mem_offset_mhz", "voltage_offset_mv", for AMD cards with a full curve "voltage_curve" (a list of {"mhz":1450,"mv":800} points, all of them), and for Intel "core_clock_min_mhz" and "core_clock_max_mhz". Values the card doesn\*(Aqt allow are refused.
.RS
\fB\-\-save\fR: Conserver les réglages après un redémarrage et exécuter les courbes de ventilateur dans le service en arrière\-plan
.RE
.RS
\fB\-\-yes\fR: Conserver les réglages sans demander de confirmation
.RE
.RS
\fB\-\-confirm\fR: Secondes d’attente de la confirmation avant d’annuler la modification
.RE
.TP
\fBvoltkit gpu forget\fR
Supprimer les réglages enregistrés d’une carte et lui rendre ses ventilateurs
.TP
\fBvoltkit gpu service\fR
Exécuter le service en arrière\-plan qui applique les réglages GPU enregistrés et suit les courbes de ventilateur
.TP
\fBvoltkit gpu record [\-\-seconds] [\-\-label] [\-\-gpu]\fR
Record the readings of a card for a while, to compare profiles later

Writes a CSV file you can open in a spreadsheet, and prints a summary with the energy used and the clock\-work each watt bought ("active MHz per watt"). Run it while a game or a benchmark is going, once per profile, then compare the sessions.
.RS
\fB\-\-seconds\fR: How many seconds to record
.RE
.RS
\fB\-\-label\fR: What is being tried, such as the profile name
.RE
.RS
\fB\-\-gpu\fR: The card\*(Aqs PCI address (the first NVIDIA or AMD card by default)
.RE
.TP
\fBvoltkit gpu check [\-\-seconds]\fR
Check Voltkit\*(Aqs readings against a second source and measure what monitoring costs

On NVIDIA cards it compares NVML, which Voltkit reads, with `nvidia\-smi` taken at the same moments, and reports how far apart they are against the accuracy targets. It also measures the CPU time and memory monitoring uses. Cards from other makers have no second source on most computers; the command says so.
.RS
\fB\-\-seconds\fR: How many seconds to compare for
.RE
.TP
\fBvoltkit gpu sessions\fR
List the recorded sessions, newest first
.TP
\fBvoltkit gpu compare\fR
Compare two recorded sessions side by side

Each session is a file, or a number from `voltkit gpu sessions`. Shows temperature, power, energy, fan speed, clocks and efficiency, and which session is better at each. Efficiency is "active MHz per watt", a proxy for work per watt; add an fps column from a tool such as MangoHud to a session file to get frames per second per watt too.
.TP
\fBvoltkit gpu profiles\fR
Named profiles that switch automatically by power source, running app, load or temperature
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
